---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Versioning - Soustack Specification">
  <h1>Versioning</h1>
  
  <div class="section">
    <h2>URL Stability</h2>
    <p>URLs for machine-readable artifacts (schemas, definitions, stacks) are stable and do not include version numbers in the path. This ensures that references remain valid over time.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h2>Breaking Changes</h2>
    <p>Breaking changes are handled via stack major versions. When a stack introduces breaking changes, it increments its major version number (e.g., from 1.x.x to 2.x.x), while the schema URLs remain unchanged.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h2>Legacy Namespaces</h2>
    <p>Older namespaces may exist as legacy aliases for backward compatibility. These are not canonical and should not be used for new implementations. See the <a href="/URL-CONTRACT.md">URL Contract</a> for details.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

